## Artwork and other assets

The MIT terms above cover the source code. They do not grant any rights in the
artwork, icons, fonts or audio distributed alongside it — those are licensed
separately or not at all, and some depict characters owned by third parties.
Do not assume asset files are MIT because this file sits next to them.

Third party components carry their own licenses, kept with the files they
belong to (for example `LICENSE.txt` beside a font, or a `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES`
file next to a vendored bundle).
